jobResponsibilities:
He or she is expected to:

a.	Support the Director and Deputy Director to:
i.	Strengthen systems governance for the social cohesion and resilience landscape;
ii.	Drive cross-agency and cross-sector strategy development and policy coordination;
iii.	Assure progress on key shifts affecting social cohesion and resilience under the agenda for the current term of Government; 
iv.	Commission and drive new workstreams to refresh policy thinking, including mitigating emerging divides and other key drivers impacting social cohesion.

b.	Support the staffing of (i) key WOG platforms and Ministerial Committees related to social cohesion and resilience, (ii) Cabinet Retreats, and (iii) related meetings at the PS-level.

c.	Provide policy support to PM, DPM and CM/SP for policy areas within their portfolio, as necessary.

agencyDescription:
The National Research Foundation (NRF) was set up on 1 January 2006 as a department under the Prime Minister's Office. It was set up to perform the following:

a) To provide secretariat support to the Research, Innovation and Enterprise Council (RIEC), chaired by the Senior Minister;

b) To coordinate the research of different agencies within the larger national framework in order to provide a coherent strategic overview and direction;

c) To develop policies and plans to implement the five strategic thrusts for the national R&D agenda; and

d) To implement national research, innovation and enterprise strategies approved by the RIEC, and to allocate funding to programmes that meet NRF's strategic objectives.

jobRequirements:
Experience working on security policy and operations and/or familiarity with the research ecosystem will be advantageous;
• Good awareness of current affairs;
• Strong analytical abilities with a broad sense of perspective;
• Excellent command of written and spoken English;
• Excellent inter-personal skills; and
• Team-player, meticulous, resourceful, able to work in a fast-paced environment and to perform under pressure.

Requirements: 
You should:
- be a quick learner, with a “can-do” attitude – able to operate in a fluid environment, pick up a wide spectrum of manpower issues, and never be shy of pushing the limits;  
• be able to appreciate and synthesise multiple perspectives from a myriad of stakeholders, across Government, industry, and the public.  
