jobResponsibilities:
As an officer in RPP/A&O, your key areas of work would include the following:

Resource and Performance Monitoring

1.	Support Science and Engineering Research Council (SERC) senior management in the governance and allocation of resources;
2.	Synthesise data and develop recommendations to support executive decision making;
3.	Review and improvement of SERC strategy, policy, operations and processes, including the improvement of SERC investments and activities;
4.	Develop specific measures of success with relevant experts;
5.	Conduct financial modelling and monitor budgets for SERC entities;
6.	Analyse and track performance of SERC entities in response to overall strategies;
7.	Develop and implementation of SERC Space and Infrastructure masterplans

Corporate Planning and Administration

1.	Support SERC senior management in key meeting platforms and monitor strategic and management issues across SERC;
2.	Organise events for SERC management for business reviews, and charting of strategic directions for SERC entities;
3.	Other administrative matters (e.g. budgets, office space, procurement, contracts and agreements)

